-- title:
--   Fixed component of a bad fibre yields a fixed minimal prime
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \geq 5$ with $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the image of the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ under coefficientwise extension of scalars along $\mathbb{Q} \to L$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \subseteq L \subseteq K$. Let $j \in K$, nonzero, whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant. Write $X = \mathrm{TwoChartModel}\,A\,K\,j$, the pushout of the two maps $X_{\mathrm{mid}} \to X_{\mathrm{fin}}$, $X_{\mathrm{mid}} \to X_\infty$ obtained by applying $\mathrm{Spec}$ to the inclusions of the subalgebra $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fin}}$ of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$ and of the analogous subalgebra for $j^{-1}$, and let $\pi = \mathrm{modelTo} : X \to \mathrm{Spec}\,A$ be the induced structure morphism. Assume given a self-isomorphism $\sigma$ of $X$ with $\sigma$ followed by $\pi$ equal to $\pi$, and an $A$-algebra endomorphism $\sigma_{\mathrm{fin}}$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fin}}$ such that $\mathrm{Spec}(\sigma_{\mathrm{fin}})$ followed by the chart immersion `ιFin` equals `ιFin` followed by $\sigma$. The conclusion asserts: for every algebraically closed field $k$ and every morphism $x : \mathrm{Spec}\,k \to \mathrm{Spec}\,A$ for which the projection $X \times_{\mathrm{Spec}\,A} \mathrm{Spec}\,k \to \mathrm{Spec}\,k$ is not smooth, and for every irreducible component $Z$ of the underlying space of that fibre product whose image under the base map of $\sigma \times \mathrm{id}$ is again $Z$, there exists a minimal prime $\mathfrak{P}$ of the ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fin}}$ generated by the maximal ideal of $A$ with $\sigma_{\mathrm{fin}}^{-1}(\mathfrak{P}) = \mathfrak{P}$.
--
--   This is the purely scheme-theoretic half of the argument that an automorphism of the integral two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a $p$-adic discrete valuation ring cannot permute the components of a non-smooth geometric fibre trivially: a component of the bad fibre left invariant by $\sigma$ produces a minimal prime of the special fibre of the $j$-finite chart algebra fixed by the induced endomorphism of that algebra. It is used by [`ModularCurve.XOneP.image_ne_of_mem_irreducibleComponents_pullback_of_not_smooth_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.image_ne_of_mem_irreducibleComponents_pullback_of_not_smooth_twoChartModel_x1_mul), and rests on properness, flatness and the fibre structure of the model together with the fact that the generic point of such a component lies in the $j$-finite chart.
-- source:
